    <item>
      <title>Trump: Huang Didn't Put National Security at Risk (Full Remarks)</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-11-16/trump-huang-didn-t-put-national-security-at-risk-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">4e3367c17f3c09bac43c4a35</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:22:06 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>President Donald Trump supported calls for Jensen Huang’s reinstatement as Nvidia’s chief executive officer and downplayed national security concerns about the ousted executive’s relationship with a woman suspected of being a Chinese spy.

“I would not mind that,” Trump told reporters Monday at the White House before leaving for his trip to Asia, when asked about the possibility of Huang returning as CEO. “A lot of people are asking Jensen, they think Jensen should go back. That certainly isn’t a bad idea.”

“We’ll meet with President Xi. He was here a month ago, and we’re also going to meet with President Putin, and we may meet with Kim Jong Un also,” Trump told reporters. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
